# width: 120
# Reordering the launcher dock (src/app/launcher_dock.zig, `moveItem`):
# an item's right-click menu carries *Move left* / *Move right* / *Move
# to start* / *Move to end* (up / down on a side strip), and the same
# four are `Alt+←` / `Alt+→` / `Alt+Home` / `Alt+End` while the item
# has the keyboard cursor. The order is written to `ui.dock.order` as
# the whole strip, `+` left out, so it survives a restart.
#
# `:dock start` anchors the run at the strip's first cell, so a row can
# be pinned by its leading `\n`. Out of the box it reads ` Browser
# Claude Code  Codex  HTTP  󲀀 New terminal  󰐕 New ` (// changed
# (railmove): the four first-party surfaces are on the strip): Browser
# at 1..11 (the glyph at 2, the word from 4), Claude Code at 12..26,
# Codex at 27..35, HTTP at 36..43, New terminal at 44..59, the `+` at
# 60..66. No click below may land on 12..35 — that would start a real
# `claude` / `codex`.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
ex dock always
ex dock start
expect screen contains "\n   Browser  󱸀 Claude Code  󱸁 Codex   HTTP  󲀀 New terminal  󰐕 New "
# Browser's menu: the four rows, worded for a bottom strip.
rightclick 5 37
expect screen contains "Move left"
expect screen contains "Move right"
expect screen contains "Move to start"
expect screen contains "Move to end"
expect screen lacks "Move up"
# *Pin to dock* is row 0, *Move left* row 1, *Move right* row 2.
key down
key down
key enter
expect screen contains "dock: Browser moved"
expect screen contains "\n  󱸀 Claude Code   Browser  󱸁 Codex   HTTP  󲀀 New terminal  󰐕 New "
# The keyboard: the cursor followed Browser to its new place, so
# `Alt+←` from `view.focus_dock` moves it straight back — and the keys
# stay in the strip, so `Alt+End` then sends it to the end of the run,
# where the `+` is still behind it. The `▸` is the cursor, in the
# padding cell before the item's glyph; it travels with Browser.
command view.focus_dock
key alt+left
expect screen contains "dock: Browser moved"
expect screen contains "\n ▸ Browser  󱸀 Claude Code  󱸁 Codex   HTTP  󲀀 New terminal  󰐕 New "
key alt+end
expect screen contains "\n  󱸀 Claude Code  󱸁 Codex   HTTP  󲀀 New terminal ▸ Browser  󰐕 New "
# Past the end is a toast, not a write.
key alt+right
expect screen contains "Browser is already at the end"
# The `+` does not move: its end is `ui.dock.plus_at`'s to give.
key end
key alt+left
expect screen contains "the + keeps its end"
expect screen contains "\n  󱸀 Claude Code  󱸁 Codex   HTTP  󲀀 New terminal   Browser ▸󰐕 New "
key esc
expect screen contains "\n  󱸀 Claude Code  󱸁 Codex   HTTP  󲀀 New terminal   Browser  󰐕 New "
# The `+`'s own menu offers no move rows at all. With Browser moved to
# the end the `+` is at 60..66, its glyph at 61.
rightclick 61 37
expect screen lacks "Move left"
expect screen contains "Show the + button"
key esc
# `Alt+Home` from the keys: back to the start.
command view.focus_dock
key end
key left
key alt+home
expect screen contains "\n ▸ Browser  󱸀 Claude Code  󱸁 Codex   HTTP  󲀀 New terminal  󰐕 New "
key esc
expect screen contains "\n   Browser  󱸀 Claude Code  󱸁 Codex   HTTP  󲀀 New terminal  󰐕 New "
